b. health and social security;
c. population administration registration;
d. opportunities to obtain skills to improve economic status; and
e. access to information and legal consultation services.

CHAPTER XII

GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 32

1. The Regent or Regional Apparatus Organization in charge of women's empowerment shall conduct guidance and supervision over women's empowerment and protection;
2. Forms of guidance as referred to in paragraph (1) are as follows:
a. providing socialization to the community and business world regarding policies on women's empowerment and protection;
b. providing books, leaflets, brochures regarding women's empowerment and protection, and other related issues and disseminating them to the community;
c facilitation of capacity building for institutions organizing women's empowerment and protection;
d. facilitation of women's participation forums and women's organizations;
e. facilitation of rehabilitation and reintegration services for women disaster victims and victims of violence;
f. coordinating the participation of the business world and other institutions, including international assistance for women's empowerment and protection; and
g. providing awards to the community and business world both individually and institutionally who have made efforts for women's empowerment and protection.
3. Forms of supervision as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of monitoring and evaluation activities over women's empowerment and protection.

